e Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/new-hampshire/carroll-county"],["ARC or PLC in Carroll County","/arc-plc/new-hampshire/carroll-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and May to June came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years. In 2025, July to August came in at 39% of normal on the middle of the grids, and August to September at 56%. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 155% of normal. Grid 28437 had its driest year in 1965, at 64% of normal.</p>"}
